# SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000163  -  CAT II
# The web server must be configurable to integrate with an organizations
# security infrastructure.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000163
group:           V-206423
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001851
control_rev5:    AU-4

contribution:    Splunk integrates with surrounding security infrastructure in two
                 configurable ways: it forwards its events onward through outputs.conf, and
                 it fires alert actions from its own health reporter. The existence of the
                 receiving security tool is not a Splunk setting.

governs:         health.conf - Thresholds for Splunk reporting on its own health.
governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.

check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server non_empty
check:           health.conf [alert_action:<action name>] disabled equals 0
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The organization's security tool that offers review and alert capability,
                 and its own ingestion configuration
external:        Whether that tool is in place at all, which the check text asks the
                 assessor to determine and no Splunk setting records
external:        Network reachability and transport between Splunk and that tool

citation:        SRG-APP-000358-WSR-000163 (V-206423) check text; SPLK-CL-000150 check and
                 fix text; outputs.conf.spec:121-131; health.conf.spec:217-219
finding:         No receiving system is configured in outputs.conf and the health
                 reporter's alert action is disabled, so the application sends its logged
                 events and alerts nowhere and is not integrated with the organization's
                 security infrastructure.
